{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch739X3ofqGEN3ec3LU5H","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I didn't include the guarantee. As far as I can tell, this email can't fund every child on the waiting list, and the claim would likely be picked apart by readers who are already wary of you.\n\n- **The cost:** 61 children × $1,150 = **$70,150**.\n- **Best case:** if all 340 lapsed donors gave their average $85, that's $28,900. With the match, it's $57,800. That's still $12,000 short.\n- **Likely case:** last year this group gave $1,240. Even at three times that, with the match, you'd raise under $8,000. That funds about six or seven children.\n\nThese are the people who left angry over Eastside. If you promise \"every child\" and the waiting list is still there in February, the former board member gets a ready-made \"they're doing it again\" note to forward. So the draft below sticks to promises you can keep: the match is real, $575 from them pays for a full year for one child, and every gift helps.\n\nBefore sending, please check:\n1. **The match terms.** Make sure the foundation counts someone whose last gift was in 2019–2022 as a \"returning donor.\" Also decide what the email says once the $15,000 is used up.\n2. **January places.** The draft says funded children \"come off the waiting list.\" Confirm that a funded child really can start in January.\n3. **Placeholders.** Fill in the name fields and the donation link.\n\nThe draft is about 200 words.\n\n<final_document>\n**Subject:** 61 kids are waiting. This month, your gift counts twice.\n\nDear [First Name],\n\nRight now, 61 children are on our waiting list for subsidized music lessons. A year of weekly lessons costs us $1,150 per child, and we can only offer a place once that year is paid for.\n\nThis December, your gift goes twice as far. A family foundation will match every gift from returning donors dollar for dollar, up to $15,000, through December 31.\n\n- $85 becomes $170\n- $575 becomes $1,150, a full year of lessons for one child\n\nWe know many of you stepped away after we closed our Eastside branch in 2022. It was a hard decision, and some of you told us plainly how it felt. You had every right to. We aren't asking you to forget it. We're asking whether you'll help one of these kids start lessons in January.\n\nEvery child we fund comes off the waiting list. Every dollar you give is doubled until the match runs out.\n\n**[Give today. Your gift will be matched.]**\n\nWith gratitude,\n\n[Executive Director Name]\nExecutive Director, [School Name]\n</final_document>"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5416,"cache_read_input_tokens":3853,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5416},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d86168dd-757d-4658-86e9-a3ad03c02635","uuid":"78a91356-838d-4d9b-918a-249c1283e9b6","timestamp":"2026-11-16T17:56:26.660Z","request_id":"req_011Ch739WYZHTKwz9EU7NdAe"}
